  "doc.title": "How Soy Sauce Gets Its Flavor · a long essay you can play with",
  "doc.desc": "Soybeans, wheat, salt and water are each bland, pale and odourless, yet half a year together turns them into soy sauce; some soy sauce is made in days. Six models you can push: a heating koji bed, the sugar wheat brings, the hand-over from lactic bacteria to yeast in brine, colour and temperature, the amino-nitrogen number on the label, and the sodium in a spoonful.",
